&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For more than 25 years, Corcept has been singularly focused on the science of cortisol, a powerful hormone that when unregulated, can play a role in a broad range of diseases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commercial portfolio includes treatments for hypercortisolism and oncology, and the company has discovered more than 1,000 proprietary selective cortisol modulators and glucocorticoid receptor antagonists. With advanced clinical trials in patients with hypercortisolism, solid tumors, ALS and liver disease, Corcept is unlocking the power of cortisol modulation to help address some of the most devastating diseases patients face today.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Corcept is headquartered in Redwood City, California. To learn more, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://nam10.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.corcept.com%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7Cgcastrence%40corcept.com%7C8262d50a280e4da5b72208de91a94917%7Cf75457eed65640339f048a7aedb19388%7C0%7C0%7C639108353411832645%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=Yc8odS9%2FPf%2B7kSorJ4ftwNYbnrVi9jKto%2BkzxHyv3ZA%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;www.corcept.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director, Europe Sales Training &amp;amp; Operations will serve as a strategic leader supporting Corcept’s Oncology expansion in Europe, with an initial focus on Germany (and the DACH region) and scalability to broader European markets. This role integrates commercial training, learning &amp;amp; development, and field operations excellence to enable a high-performing, launch-ready organization. This role will report to the Europe General Manager (or, if a GM is not in place at the time of hiring, the President of Oncology).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This individual will design and operationalize capabilities across the commercial ecosystem, ensuring alignment of training, field execution, processes, and performance enablement with brand strategy and launch priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commercial Training &amp;amp; Capability Building&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the strategy, design, and execution of comprehensive commercial learning programs, including onboarding, product and disease state training, competitive intelligence, and selling skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement scalable learning frameworks that support launch readiness and ongoing capability development in Germany and broader Europe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Sales, Marketing, Market Access, Medical Affairs, Legal and Compliance to ensure training strategies align with brand objectives, market dynamics, and regional business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish coaching standards and field development processes in partnership with local field leadership to identify capability gaps, reinforce key behaviors, and drive field excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Field Operations &amp;amp; Commercial Execution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational excellence through the development and continuous improvement of commercial processes, technologies, and field support systems that enable execution at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead onboarding operations and field readiness strategies to accelerate new hire productivity and ensure consistent employee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct the planning and execution of key commercial initiatives, national and regional meetings, and recognition programs that reinforce strategic priorities and organizational culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor relationships, budgets, and operational planning to ensure compliant, efficient, and fiscally responsible execution across commercial initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learning Infrastructure &amp;amp; Insights&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee Learning Management System (LMS) strategy, including vendor selection, implementation, governance, and continued optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish performance metrics and analytics to assess training effectiveness, learner adoption, and impact on field performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture field insights through engagement, field visits, and stakeholder feedback to inform training strategies, operational improvements, and business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Communication&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive structured communication and meeting cadences to ensure alignment, transparency, and engagement across the European commercial organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute field communication strategies that drive awareness, adoption, and alignment around key business initiatives, training programs, and organizational priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic partner to regional leadership, contributing to planning, execution, and continuous improvement initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a culture of collaboration, accountability, and strategic execution, setting high standards for leadership effectiveness and cross-functional partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills, Qualifications and Technical Proficiencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence with the ability to influence senior stakeholders and drive cross-functional alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage complex projects, vendors, and budgets while driving measurable business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Education and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in pharmaceutical or biotech commercial roles, including sales, training, or field operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting launch or expansion in international markets; Europe (Germany/DACH) experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success integrating commercial training, field enablement, and operational excellence in a matrixed environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language: English fluency required, German fluency preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For information on how Corcept collects, uses, discloses, protects, and otherwise processes personal information and an explanation of the rights and choices available to you with respect to your personal information, please refer to our &lt;a href=&quot;https://corcept.com/privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice link&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Corcept appreciates the commitment and hard work of all our team members as we strive to discover and develop novel treatments for patients with serious unmet medical needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please visit our website at: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.corcept.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.corcept.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corcept is an Equal Opportunity Employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Corcept will not conduct interviews via text message or messaging platforms and will not ask you to download anything as part of your interview.&amp;nbsp; Though we use third-party tools to help with advertising our jobs, please be vigilant in checking that the communication is in fact coming from Corcept.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
